    "explanation": "$x_2 = \\frac{3 + 5}{4 - 3} = 8$. The gradient $f'(1) = 1$ is small compared with $f(1) = -7$, so the tangent meets the axis far beyond the root (the curve has a turning point near $x = 0.91$).",
    "workedSolution": "1. $x_2 = \\frac{3 + 5}{4 - 3} = 8$. The gradient $f'(1) = 1$ is small compared with $f(1) = -7$, so the tangent meets the axis far beyond the root (the curve has a turning point near $x = 0.91$)."
